  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "releaseNotes": "1.15.0-preview.3: GA-readiness. The bundled nginx is upgraded to the 1.30 stable branch (1.30.2) from 1.24.0 — a newer branch with a smaller CVE backlog. The sidecar now ships a PR_SET_PDEATHSIG launch shim so the bundled nginx can't be orphaned (and keep holding the listen port) if the host process is hard-killed (SIGKILL/OOM/container hard-stop); it derives the bundled runtime identifier at runtime so the matched nginx resolves on linux-arm64 as well as linux-x64; and it emits a per-RID build-info.json provenance manifest. The native engine still targets a glibc 2.31 floor with statically-linked libstdc++ and no OpenSSL host dependency, so it loads on Debian 11/12, Ubuntu 20.04+, RHEL/Alma 8/9 and Amazon Linux 2023. A single `dotnet add package` auto-pulls the native engine; binaries are stripped (debug archived separately). mod_pagespeed 1.15 as an ASP.NET Core sidecar that runs a bundled, matched (nginx + ngx_pagespeed) reverse proxy in front of your Kestrel app (ADR-085). Linux-only (linux-x64, linux-arm64). Experimental preview; API may change before GA.",
